id: torchlit
name: Torchlit
kind: conditions
# One stack per lit Torch in hand: each is a Light Source of its own.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry makes its holder a Light Source and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# A Level up per stack. Read by `lightLevelOf`, which names no mark.
lightShift: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  You are holding a lit Torch. Your Light Level is a Level higher.
text: >
  Torchlit: the Torch's mark. "While you are holding a Torch, you are a Light Source.
  Increase the Light Level of all Squares within a Sphere AoE (centered on you) by 1 Level."

---

# Brightened's shape with no clock: it lasts as long as the Torch burns, and is taken off when
# it is put out, stored in a Capsule, or taken off the character. The holder's own Square is
# in the Sphere, so theirs is raised here; everyone else's is the table's.
#
# No effects of its own: what a Light Level does is in that Level's own file.
